cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QSOL UFF, cite this software and the primary papers for every model used."
title: "QSOL UFF v4.0.0: Galaxy Dynamics and Compact-Object Research Laboratory"
type: software
version: 4.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-14
authors:
  - family-names: Slade
    given-names: Trent
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-4515-9237"
repository-code: "https://github.com/QSOLKCB/UFF"
url: "https://github.com/QSOLKCB/UFF"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.17669627"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - galaxy rotation curves
  - SPARC
  - MOND
  - radial acceleration relation
  - NFW
  - Burkert
  - supermassive black holes
  - loop quantum gravity
abstract: >-
  A transparent Python laboratory for validated SPARC-style galaxy data,
  dimensionally explicit baryonic, halo, MOND/RAR, SMBH, and empirical UFF
  rotation-curve models, deterministic model comparison, and separately scoped
  Kerr/LQG compact-object scale diagnostics.
